    </p><a href="/">← Home</a><pagefind-searchbox></pagefind-searchbox><script type="module" src="/pagefind/pagefind-component-ui.js"></script><script type="text/javascript" src="/static/pagefind.js"></script><h1 class="instruction-section" data-pagefind-body="1" data-pagefind-weight="10" data-pagefind-sort="title">UCVTF (scalar, integer)</h1><p class="insn_subtitle" data-pagefind-body="1">Unsigned integer convert to floating-point (scalar)</p>
      <p class="aml" data-pagefind-body="1">This instruction converts the unsigned integer value
in the general-purpose source register to a
floating-point value using the rounding mode that is specified by the
FPCR, and
writes the result to the SIMD&amp;FP destination register.</p>
      <p class="aml" data-pagefind-body="1">This instruction can generate a floating-point exception.
  Depending on the settings in FPCR,
  the exception results in either a flag being set in FPSR
  or a synchronous exception being generated.
  For more information, see
  <a class="armarm-xref" title="Reference to Armv8 ARM section" data-linkend="BEIJDDAG">Floating-point exceptions and exception traps</a>.</p>
      <p class="aml" data-pagefind-body="1">Depending on the settings in the CPACR_EL1,
  CPTR_EL2, and CPTR_EL3 registers,
  and the current Security state and Exception level,
  an attempt to execute the instruction might be trapped.</p>
    
